{"summary":"The amendment does not hold up against the current implementation: the rooted-plant substrate oxygenation hook is present, wired into downstream substrate/nitrogen behavior, instrumented, and covered by dedicated tests, so this reads like an outdated description of an alkalinity-only diff.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-8-00f5463d","decision":"reject","rationale":"Reject. `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate.rs` implements the rooted-plant hook directly: it computes habitat-aware active rooted biomass, excludes non-rooted/floating plants, applies a saturating `rol_rate_cm_per_g` bonus to substrate O2 penetration depth, and writes the effective penetration back to substrate layers. The habitat-registry coupling the amendment says is missing is present via `substrate_root_activity_factor(...)`, which queries `SubstrateSurface` and `SubstrateDeep` areas. That changed penetration depth feeds downstream behavior: `crates/tank_core/src/types/habitat.rs` derives `SubstrateSurface` area from the oxic zone, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs` uses suboxic pore volume for denitrification, and nitrifier carrying capacity is habitat-area based. `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` also exposes root-oxygenation metrics/notes in tracing and budgets. Dedicated coverage exists in `crates/tank_core/tests/root_zone_oxygenation.rs` and substrate unit tests, and `cargo test -p tank_core --test root_zone_oxygenation --test nitrification_alkalinity` passes. The `plant_growth.rs` comment is stale documentation, not evidence that the feature is absent."}]}